{"content":[{"c":["JAPHIA (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. King of Lachish who joined an alliance of four other Amorite kings to punish Gibeon for its treaty with the Jews. Joshua dealt a total defeat to the Amorites at the battle of Beth-horon (aided by hailstones and the sun standing still). Japhia and the four kings hid in a cave at Makkedah but were discovered and hung by Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.3-27","r":"Josh.10.3-27","rawR":"Josh.10.3-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.3-27","value":"Josh.10.3-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:3-27"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Son born to David while he was king in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.15","r":"2Sam.5.15","rawR":"2Sam.5.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.15","value":"2Sam.5.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.7","r":"1Chr.3.7","rawR":"1Chr.3.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.7","value":"1Chr.3.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.14.6","r":"1Chr.14.6","rawR":"1Chr.14.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.14.6","value":"1Chr.14.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JaphiaPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 10:3-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.3-27","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.3-27","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.3-27"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.15","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.15","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.7"},{"anchorText":"14:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExa